// Probe 14 — Cluster I LHS border: method-call result `s.method() ?? "x"`
//
// `s.to_uppercase()` resolves to the bounded-generic stub
// `t_<len>text_to_uppercase` which returns text from its own work
// buffer.  Stub returns go through the @P205 scratch-routing logic in
// src/generation/emit.rs:1212-1262 (the `needs_p205_scratch` path).
// If that scratch-routing applies on the INTERPRETER path too, the
// consumer reads from `stores.scratch` (program-lifetime) rather than a
// block-local, and 14 PASSES.
//
// If 14 FAILS, the @P205 work-buffer protection is native-only and
// cluster I extends to method-call returns.
//
// Pairing: diff against 05 (raw call) — same shape via the method-call
// dispatch path.
// Status: cluster I LHS-border probe; tests dispatch-mechanism independence.

fn main() {
  s = "present";
  a = s.to_uppercase() ?? "fallback";
  assert(a == "PRESENT", "probe 14: got '{a}', want 'PRESENT'");
  println("probe 14 PASSED");
}
